Package: cytome
Type: Package
Title: Native R Reader and Streaming Interface for the Cytome Single-Cell Store
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Min", "Dai", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dai@broadinstitute.org"),
    person("PIASO Team", role = "cph"))
Description: Reads .cytome files - a SQLite-backed single-cell store - natively in R with
    zero Python dependency. A .cytome is a plain SQLite database, so the structural data
    (cells / genes / peaks, embeddings, graphs, fragments) is read with DBI; the chunked,
    compressed CSR count matrices are decoded via a small Rcpp layer (lz4-block / zstd / zlib).
    Constructs a SingleCellExperiment or a Seurat object, and provides cytome-native chunk
    streaming for out-of-core analysis without loading the full matrix.
    Part of the PIASO toolkit for single-cell omics (<https://piaso.org>).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/genecell/cytome-r, https://piaso.org
BugReports: https://github.com/genecell/cytome-r/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
